body:
This PR adds Python/JSON style syntax support for STRUCT and LIST entries, i.e. the following statements are now valid:

```sql
SELECT {'i': 3, 'j': 4};
-- equivalent to STRUCT_PACK(i := 3, j := 4)
SELECT [1,2,3];
-- equivalent to LIST_VALUE(1, 2, 3)
SELECT {'i': [1,2, 3], 'j': 4};
-- equivalent to STRUCT_PACK(i := LIST_VALUE(1,2,3), j := 4)

-- quotes are optional
SELECT {i: 3, j: 4};
-- double quotes are also allowed
SELECT {"i": 3, "j": 4};
```

This PR also changes the struct -> string conversion to follow the same style, so the string conversion can be round-tripped easily:

```sql
SELECT {'i': 3, 'j': 4}::VARCHAR;
-- {'i': 3, 'j': 4}
```
